# Hooks and Store

- Name hooks `useSomething` and keep them in `hooks/` or `store/` folders (e.g. `src/features/auth/store/auth.store.ts`, `src/features/events/hooks`) – never bury hooks in generic util files.
- Shared app or feature state must live in explicit store or context hooks (like the auth store and events context), not in ad-hoc module-level singletons.
- When state needs to survive reloads, plug into the existing localStorage-backed store abstractions instead of hand-rolling new persistence logic.
- Use `useReducer` for complex, event-driven state (forms, wizards, modals) and keep reducer logic in `*.reducer.ts` files colocated with the hook or component.
- Do not introduce new global state libraries (Redux, Zustand, MobX, etc.); extend the existing custom store + context patterns instead.
- Keep hook responsibilities tight: one hook should solve one concern – if a hook is doing everything (data fetching, business logic, UI decisions), split it up.
